      "message": "tl;dr: This is fine, but raises a couple questions about how to improve on SkLog.\n\nTalked offline about this, but for record keeping: SkLog is ideally not directly called in production. Since dm is a tool and not core Skia, this one use case is fine.\nThis does bring up the question of whether we should:\n1) Expose an \"SK_LOG_ALWAYS\" macro\n2) Not force the [skia] tag on every log (or allow custom tags)\n\nSkLog was primarily developed with clients in mind (Chrome, Android, etc.) that might want to filter out logs based on library/module and priority, but in cases where Skia is all of it, I can see [skia] showing up on each line as too busy.",
